# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the host KV tier SHIP-CANDIDATE gates (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# tp4/prefix-tiers and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Templates only: no tag is pushed from the
# branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the pass rule. ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-tier-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed tp4/prefix-tiers head
# (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-tier-1/<tag>/' *.env). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# TC1 (STOP): the AUDITED CONCURRENT arm (c2_prefix_gate.py --plan tier-concurrent, scenario tier_concurrent) on the ship candidate's gate-only audit twin c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-tierfx-audit: the fusion programme's combined audit arm
# (every lever of the ship candidate plus its _AUDIT flag) plus the tier with every instrument on (each restored block read back and compared, each block's digest checked at restore, the preconverted tensors compared with
# today's conversion, the multi launch's own SDPA audit). Sequence (prefix_replay.scenario_tier_concurrent): a session built to the largest size the profile admits, fresh-salt floods the size of the KV pool so that it
# leaves the device pool for host RAM, SEVEN SEATS decoding (about 4k-token coding prompts, ignore_eos, 60,000 tokens of budget), a 10 s settle and a 60 s CONTROL window of the seats alone, then the session RETURNS
# (restored from host RAM; it decodes 512 tokens beside the seats as an eighth seat), a long (120k) fresh prompt (SPILL: its blocks displace cached ones, which the tier reads out), and the returning turn's COLD TWIN
# (a fresh salt, the same body; strict pair). READ: the plan verdict PASS: every pair IDENTICAL (the restored answer against its cold twin), a 'host tier restore' line for the returning turn at the oracle's Q, 'host tier
# spill' lines inside the long prompt's request, the failure counters (spill, restore, digest, read-back mismatch) ZERO, no pins held, every one of the seven seats decoding across the control, restore, restore_decode and
# spill windows (else NOT_EXERCISED), and the lines 'window <name>: ... round time p50/p99/mean ..., longest wait ... s, round p99 vs control ...%'. The stall is PRINTED here, not judged (the audits are this arm's
# cost); the budget is judged on TC2 to TC5. The seats' text is compared with the control boot by TC2 to TC5, not here. Unqualified: a measurement, never evidence. Duration (estimate; nothing of this scenario has run
# on a card: the floods at the production pool and the audited arm's cost are the unmeasured parts): 90 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-tier-1
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=tier-concurrent
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-tierfx-audit
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_BOX_MINUTES=150
